{"name":"Creamy Strawberry","hex":"#fcd2df","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"creamy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing cream.","Of food or drink, having the rich taste or thick, smooth texture of cream, whether or not it actually contains cream."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A horse with a cream-coloured coat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creamy"},{"term":"strawberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sweet, usually red, edible accessory fruit of certain plants of the genus Fragaria.","Any plant of the genus Fragaria (that bears such fruit)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor of strawberries.","Flavored with ethyl methylphenylglycidate, an artificial compound which is said to resemble the taste of strawberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fragaria viridis","blocks":[{"text":"Fragaria viridis, commonly called creamy strawberry or green strawberry, is a species of strawberry native to Europe and central Asia. It has fruits with fine flavour. They have surprisingly little of the usual strawberry aroma, but a refreshing acidity, and sometimes ripen without becoming red. When they are plucked from the plant, the calyx will usually adhere and they will detach with a noticeable snapping sound."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Fragaria-viridis.JPG/330px-Fragaria-viridis.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fragaria_viridis","wikidata":"Q148663"},{"title":"Creamy","blocks":[{"text":"Creamy were a Danish-Faroese teen-pop duo, composed of Rebekka Mathew and Rannva Joensen."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creamy","wikidata":"Q5183392"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry","wikidata":"Q13158"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%28Fragaria_viridis%29.jpeg/120px-%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%28Fragaria_viridis%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%28Fragaria_viridis%29.jpeg/250px-%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%28Fragaria_viridis%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%28Fragaria_viridis%29.jpeg/120px-%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%28Fragaria_viridis%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_(Fragaria_viridis).jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/%D0%9A%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%BB